    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are prioritizing high-upside matchups today, led by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) and **Christian Yelich** (74.33). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our premier start, leveraging a favorable matchup against Kyle Leahy to exploit his elite speed, which remains our primary objective in this 5x5 format. **Christian Yelich** also earns a strong recommendation; despite a minor BvP concern, he benefits from a soft matchup against Merrill Kelly, where a high SP_xERA (5.47) and favorable platoon splits drive his efficiency score well above the floor. **Trea Turner** (67.06) and **Kyle Schwarber** (66.71) remain core pieces of our offensive engine, as both hold strong projections despite the presence of Michael Wacha.\n\nPlatoon advantages and park factors are heavily influencing our utility spots today. **Casey Schmitt** (63.20) sees a significant boost (+11% for platoon; +14% for park) against Tomoyuki Sugano, making him a mandatory start over deeper bench options. Meanwhile, **Caleb Durbin** (65.79) is positioned to capitalize on Sam Aldegheri\u2019s high xERA, providing the speed floor we require despite facing a tough catcher. **Junior Caminero** (62.88) rounds out the high-confidence starters; his ability to drive the ball against Hunter Brown keeps him in the lineup over **Josh Smith** (57.17). **Josh Smith** was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine, but his slightly lower raw base projection kept him sidelined in favor of the more favorable platoon matchup afforded to **Casey Schmitt**.\n\nWe are proceeding with caution regarding our \"Lineup Pending\" designations, particularly with **Gary Sanchez** (56.03) and **Dillon Dingler** (47.45). While **Gary Sanchez** benefits from a poor matchup for Merrill Kelly, his utility is highly sensitive to his batting order\u2014a late-day shuffle to the bottom of the order could dampen his output. **Dillon Dingler** carries our lowest score among starters; he is a marginal play who survives only because his matchup against Kumar Rocker offers enough potential for stolen base upside due to the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery. We will monitor these slots closely as the official lineups release, specifically watching for any weather-related risks that might necessitate a late pivot to **Nelson Velazquez** or **Lars Nootbaar** from our bench.",
